IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- The Income Tax Act, 2000 (Saskatchewan), S.S. 2000, c. I-2.01 -- the tax on an individual for the 2026 taxation year:
-- who must pay (s 6); taxable income (s 7, taken from the federal return); the rates (s 8, with the 2026 thresholds);
-- the Division 2 non-refundable credits most people claim (ss 11, 12, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23, 28) and the basic tax
-- they leave; the Saskatchewan low-income tax credit (s 39, with The Saskatchewan Low-income Tax Credit Regulations, s 3);
-- the duty to pay by the balance-due day (s 81) and to file (s 75, adopting federal s 150); the protection of the
-- low-income credit refund from creditors (s 40).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer. "Must I pay Saskatchewan tax? How much? What credits do I get, and how much low-income
-- tax credit will be paid to me, and when? By when must I file and pay?" Provisions addressed to the minister (who, under
-- the collection agreement of s 68, is the federal Minister of National Revenue: s 2(s)) are encoded as what they mean for
-- that person.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION. The statutory text quoted in the comments is reproduced, for non-commercial use, from the
-- consolidation of the Office of the King's Printer for Saskatchewan (Publications Centre), last update posted
-- 16 Sep 2026; it is not an official version. (c) 2026, Government of Saskatchewan. The 2026 bracket thresholds are from
-- the Canada Revenue Agency page "Current year tax rates and income brackets (2026)", a copy of the version available at
-- https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/individuals/tax-rates-brackets/current-year.html (see
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/cra-tax-rates-brackets-2026.txt and SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- Federal figures are inputs: taxable income (federal Part I), income for the year, net income of a spouse or dependant,
-- the federal s 118.7 CPP/EI amount, the federal s 118(3) pension amount, adjusted income under federal s 122.5. Read
-- with the federal Income Tax Act encoding, subjects/ca/income-tax-act/ (cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the
-- stable l4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answers `not covered` where a question can reach it): taxation years other than 2026 (their amounts are
-- either stated for other years or left to CPI indexation under s 51(3)); trusts (s 9); the credits of ss 14, 15, 16,
-- 19.1-19.5, 22, 24-27, 29 and Division 3 (an input total); the impairment credit supplement for a child (s 23(2.4));
-- minimum tax and tax on split income (Division 6); part-year residents (s 44); the refundable credits other than s 39.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The Income Tax Act, 2000 -- personal income tax of an individual, 2026`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `only the 2026 taxation year is encoded`
    `a trust is taxed under s 9, which is not encoded`
    `the individual is not liable to tax under s 6(1): not resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year and no income earned in Saskatchewan`
    `the individual is exempt from tax under s 6(2) (federal s 149(1))`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` x y MEANS IF x AT LEAST y THEN x ELSE y

-- "the amount, if any, by which x exceeds y"
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess of` x `over` y MEANS `the greater of` 0 (x MINUS y)

GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taxation year is encoded` IF `taxation year` EQUALS 2026

§§ `s 5(1)(a), s 8(1) -- the rates`

-- s 5(1)(a): "'appropriate percentage' means, with respect to a taxation year, the percentage set out in clause 8(1)(a)":
-- 10.5%. Every Division 2 credit is the appropriate percentage times a dollar amount.
`the appropriate percentage` MEANS 10.5%

-- s 8(1)(c): the top rate, 14.5%; s 21(3) uses it ("C is the percentage set out in clause 8(1)(c)").
`the top rate` MEANS 14.5%

-- s 8(1): "(a) 10.5% of the taxable income if the taxable income does not exceed $45,225; (b) the maximum amount determined
-- pursuant to clause (a) plus 12.5% of the amount by which the taxable income exceeds $45,225 if the taxable income exceeds
-- $45,225 but does not exceed $129,214; or (c) the maximum amount determined pursuant to clause (b) plus 14.5% of the amount
-- by which the taxable income exceeds $129,214". s 8(2): "For the 2021 and subsequent taxation years, subsection (1)
-- applies, subject to the dollar amounts mentioned in that subsection being adjusted in accordance with subsection 51(3)."
-- The CPI indexation of s 51(3) is not in the deposited text. The 2026 thresholds are taken from the deposited CRA page
-- ($54,532 and $155,805); the first is confirmed by Reg 7 s 3, whose "$54,532" is MB, "the dollar value for the taxation
-- year as determined in clause 8(1)(a), subject to subsection 8(2)" (Act s 39(6.3)). NOTES.md finding 1.
`the 2026 first threshold` MEANS 54532
`the 2026 second threshold` MEANS 155805

GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8(1) tax for 2026` `taxable income` MEANS
          (10.5% TIMES (`the lesser of` `taxable income` `the 2026 first threshold`))
    PLUS  (12.5% TIMES (`the excess of` (`the lesser of` `taxable income` `the 2026 second threshold`) `over` `the 2026 first threshold`))
    PLUS  (14.5% TIMES (`the excess of` `taxable income` `over` `the 2026 second threshold`))

§§ `s 6 -- who must pay`

-- s 6(1): "(a) every individual who is resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of a taxation year and has no income earned
-- in the taxation year outside Saskatchewan; (b) every individual who is resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of a
-- taxation year and has income earned in the taxation year outside Saskatchewan; (c) every individual who is not resident
-- in Saskatchewan on the last day of a taxation year but has income earned in the taxation year in Saskatchewan."
-- "Income earned in the taxation year in Saskatchewan" is defined through the federal regulations (s 5(1)(b)); it is
-- asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Liability under s 6(1)` IS ONE OF
    `liable under s 6(1)(a)`
    `liable under s 6(1)(b)`
    `liable under s 6(1)(c)`
    `not liable under s 6(1)`

GIVEN `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `income earned in the year outside Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER
      `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Liability under s 6(1)`
`the s 6(1) category` `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` `income earned in the year outside Saskatchewan` `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` MEANS
    IF `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year`
    THEN IF `income earned in the year outside Saskatchewan` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `liable under s 6(1)(b)`
         ELSE `liable under s 6(1)(a)`
    ELSE IF `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `liable under s 6(1)(c)`
         ELSE `not liable under s 6(1)`

§§ `s 7, s 8(3) -- the tax on taxable income`

-- s 7: "An individual's taxable income for the purposes of this Act is: (a) the individual's taxable income for the
-- purposes of computing tax payable pursuant to Part I of the federal Act; or (b) in the case of an individual to whom
-- Division D of Part I of the federal Act applies, the individual's taxable income earned in Canada." Either way it comes
-- from the federal return, and is an input.
--
-- s 8(3): for an individual in s 6(1)(b) or (c), "T = TS x A / B" where TS is the s 8(1)/(2) tax as if the individual were
-- in s 6(1)(a), "A is the individual's income earned in the taxation year in Saskatchewan; and B is the individual's income
-- for the year."
GIVEN `category` IS A `Liability under s 6(1)`
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER
      `income for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 8 tax for 2026` `category` `taxable income` `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` `income for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `category`
    WHEN `liable under s 6(1)(a)` THEN `the s 8(1) tax for 2026` `taxable income`
    WHEN `not liable under s 6(1)` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE
        IF `income for the year` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN (`the s 8(1) tax for 2026` `taxable income`) TIMES (`income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` DIVIDED BY `income for the year`)
        ELSE 0

§§ `Division 2 -- non-refundable credits, 2026`

-- s 11(3)(b): "for the 2026 taxation year: A = AP x TCA where: AP is the appropriate percentage for the taxation year; and
-- TCA is $20,381".
`the s 11 basic personal credit for 2026` MEANS `the appropriate percentage` TIMES 20381

-- s 12(3)(b): for an individual described in paragraph (a) of the description of B in federal s 118(1) (married or in a
-- common-law partnership and supporting the spouse -- a borrowed term, asked as a fact): "B = AP x TCA ... TCA = $20,381
-- - (SI - $2,038) where SI is the greater of: (i) $2,038; and (ii) either: (A) the income for the year of the individual's
-- spouse or common-law partner; or (B) [on breakdown of the relationship] the income for the year of the spouse ... while
-- married or in the common-law partnership and not so separated". The text sets no floor; a TCA below zero is read as nil
-- (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `spouse's income for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 12 spousal credit for 2026` `spouse's income for the year` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 (20381 MINUS ((`the greater of` 2038 `spouse's income for the year`) MINUS 2038)))

-- s 13(3)(b): for an individual described in paragraph (b) of the description of B in federal s 118(1) (the eligible
-- dependant claim) "who does not claim a spousal credit pursuant to section 12": "C = AP x TCA ... TCA = $20,381 - (EI -
-- $2,038) where: EI is the greater of: (i) $2,038; and (ii) the income for the year of the person with respect to whom the
-- equivalent-to-spouse credit is being claimed".
GIVEN `dependant's income for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 13 equivalent-to-spouse credit for 2026` `dependant's income for the year` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 (20381 MINUS ((`the greater of` 2038 `dependant's income for the year`) MINUS 2038)))

-- s 17(1), (2): for an individual who "before the end of the taxation year, has attained the age of 65 years": "G = AP x
-- TCA ... TCA is [($4,894 - B)] where B is 15% of the amount, if any, by which the individual's income for the year would
-- exceed $36,430", both dollar amounts adjusted under s 51(3) for 2021 on. The 2026 adjusted amounts are not in the
-- deposited text and are inputs (NOTES.md finding 2). Income is read without s 79 gains and federal s 20(1)(ww)
-- deductions ((a), (b)); the input is that income.
GIVEN `age at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
      `income for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2026 age amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2026 age income threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 17 age credit` `age at the end of the year` `income for the year` `the 2026 age amount` `the 2026 age income threshold` MEANS
    IF `age at the end of the year` AT LEAST 65
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 (`the 2026 age amount` MINUS (15% TIMES (`the excess of` `income for the year` `over` `the 2026 age income threshold`))))
    ELSE 0

-- s 18(1): for "an individual resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the taxation year": "H = AP x B ... B is the
-- lesser of $1,000 and the amount calculated in accordance with paragraph (b) of the description of B in subsection 118(3)
-- of the federal Act" (the eligible pension income, a federal figure). Not indexed.
GIVEN `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 18 pension credit` `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount` MEANS
    IF `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES (`the lesser of` 1000 `the federal s 118(3) pension income amount`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 19(1.1): the dependent child credit is for an individual who, on the last day of the year, "(a) does not have a
-- cohabiting spouse or common-law partner as defined in section 122.6 of the federal Act; (b) has a cohabiting spouse ...
-- whose taxable income for the taxation year is greater than the individual's taxable income ...; or (c) has a cohabiting
-- spouse ... whose taxable income ... is equal to the individual's taxable income ... and the cohabiting spouse ...
-- renounces his or her entitlement". So between cohabiting spouses the lower-income one claims.
GIVEN `has a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `my cohabiting spouse's taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `my cohabiting spouse renounces the credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(1.1) lets me claim the dependent child credit` IF
        (NOT `has a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the year`)
    OR  `my cohabiting spouse's taxable income` GREATER THAN `my taxable income`
    OR  (    `my cohabiting spouse's taxable income` EQUALS `my taxable income`
         AND `my cohabiting spouse renounces the credit`)

-- s 19(4)(b): "for the 2026 taxation year: I = AP x Y x QD where: AP = the appropriate percentage ...; Y is $8,358; and QD
-- is the number of children to whom subsection (2) applies" -- (2): each child "(a) is residing with the individual on the
-- last day of the taxation year or [on the date of the child's death]; and (b) is a qualified dependant, as defined in
-- section 122.6 of the federal Act, of the individual at any time during the taxation year" (a borrowed term: the count is
-- asked as a fact). (3): no credit for a child for whom the individual claims the s 13 credit. (4): only for an individual
-- "resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the taxation year".
GIVEN `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 19(1.1) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `children to whom s 19(2) applies` IS A NUMBER
      `of them, children for whom I claim the s 13 credit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 19 dependent child credit for 2026` `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` `s 19(1.1) is met` `children to whom s 19(2) applies` `of them, children for whom I claim the s 13 credit` MEANS
    IF `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` AND `s 19(1.1) is met`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES 8358 TIMES (`the excess of` `children to whom s 19(2) applies` `over` `of them, children for whom I claim the s 13 credit`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 20(1.2)(b): "for the 2026 taxation year: J = AP x $2,569"; (2): for an individual "(a) who is resident in Saskatchewan
-- on the last day of the taxation year and has attained the age of 65 years before the end of the taxation year; or (b) who
-- dies during the taxation year, is resident in Saskatchewan on the date of death and has attained the age of 65 years
-- before the date of death". The resident-on-the-date-of-death case is asked as residence on the last day.
GIVEN `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `age at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 20 senior supplementary credit for 2026` `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` `age at the end of the year` MEANS
    IF `resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year` AND `age at the end of the year` AT LEAST 65
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES 2569
    ELSE 0

-- s 21(3): "CC = (A x B) + [C x (D - B)] where: A is the appropriate percentage ...; B is the lesser of $200 and the
-- individual's total gifts for the taxation year; C is the percentage set out in clause 8(1)(c); and D is the individual's
-- total gifts for the taxation year." (4): the total gifts claimed must be the same as on the federal return.
GIVEN `total gifts claimed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 21 gifts credit` `total gifts claimed` MEANS
    LET b MEANS `the lesser of` 200 (`the greater of` 0 `total gifts claimed`)
    IN  (`the appropriate percentage` TIMES b) PLUS (`the top rate` TIMES ((`the greater of` 0 `total gifts claimed`) MINUS b))

-- s 23: for an individual "eligible for a deduction pursuant to subsection 118.3(1) of the federal Act" (the disability
-- tax credit, a federal status asked as a fact): K = AP x TCA. For 2025 TCA is $13,986 (s 23(2.2)); for 2026 it is that
-- figure adjusted under s 51(3), which is not in the deposited text, so the 2026 TCA is an input (NOTES.md finding 2).
GIVEN `eligible for the federal s 118.3(1) disability deduction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the 2026 impairment amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 23 impairment credit` `eligible for the federal s 118.3(1) disability deduction` `the 2026 impairment amount` MEANS
    IF `eligible for the federal s 118.3(1) disability deduction`
    THEN `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `the 2026 impairment amount`
    ELSE 0

-- s 28: "a credit with respect to premiums pursuant to the Employment Insurance Act (Canada) and contributions pursuant to
-- the Canada Pension Plan in an amount determined in accordance with section 118.7 of the federal Act". Federal s 118.7 is
-- "the appropriate percentage" times the premiums and base contributions, and s 5(2) reads "appropriate percentage" in an
-- adopted federal provision as Saskatchewan's 10.5%. The amount federal s 118.7 multiplies is an input.
GIVEN `CPP base contributions and EI premiums counted by federal s 118.7` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 28 EI and CPP credit` `CPP base contributions and EI premiums counted by federal s 118.7` MEANS
    `the appropriate percentage` TIMES `CPP base contributions and EI premiums counted by federal s 118.7`

-- The Division 2 credits deduct "in computing the tax payable" and are not refundable; their total cannot take the tax below
-- nil. The order of s 49 matters only to which credits are used when they exceed the tax; the total is what the
-- individual pays on. Credits not encoded (ss 14-16, 19.1-19.5, 22, 24-27, 29, and Division 3) come in as one input.
DECLARE `Division 2 credits for 2026` HAS
    `s 11 basic personal`        IS A NUMBER
    `s 12 spousal`               IS A NUMBER
    `s 13 equivalent-to-spouse`  IS A NUMBER
    `s 17 age`                   IS A NUMBER
    `s 18 pension`               IS A NUMBER
    `s 19 dependent child`       IS A NUMBER
    `s 20 senior supplementary`  IS A NUMBER
    `s 21 gifts`                 IS A NUMBER
    `s 23 impairment`            IS A NUMBER
    `s 28 EI and CPP`            IS A NUMBER
    `other credits not encoded`  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS A `Division 2 credits for 2026`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of the credits` c MEANS
      c's `s 11 basic personal` PLUS c's `s 12 spousal` PLUS c's `s 13 equivalent-to-spouse` PLUS c's `s 17 age`
    PLUS c's `s 18 pension` PLUS c's `s 19 dependent child` PLUS c's `s 20 senior supplementary` PLUS c's `s 21 gifts`
    PLUS c's `s 23 impairment` PLUS c's `s 28 EI and CPP` PLUS c's `other credits not encoded`

GIVEN `s 8 tax` IS A NUMBER, `total credits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax after non-refundable credits` `s 8 tax` `total credits` MEANS `the excess of` `s 8 tax` `over` `total credits`

-- The whole computation, with the questions this encoding cannot answer answered `not covered`.
GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exempt under federal s 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `category` IS A `Liability under s 6(1)`
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` IS A NUMBER
      `income for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `credits` IS A `Division 2 credits for 2026`
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the Saskatchewan tax after non-refundable credits` `taxation year` `is a trust` `exempt under federal s 149(1)` `category` `taxable income` `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` `income for the year` `credits` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the taxation year is encoded` `taxation year`)
    THEN `not covered` `only the 2026 taxation year is encoded`
    ELSE IF `is a trust`
         THEN `not covered` `a trust is taxed under s 9, which is not encoded`
         ELSE IF `exempt under federal s 149(1)`
              THEN `not covered` `the individual is exempt from tax under s 6(2) (federal s 149(1))`
              ELSE IF `category` EQUALS `not liable under s 6(1)`
                   THEN `not covered` `the individual is not liable to tax under s 6(1): not resident in Saskatchewan on the last day of the year and no income earned in Saskatchewan`
                   ELSE `answered` (`the tax after non-refundable credits` (`the s 8 tax for 2026` `category` `taxable income` `income earned in the year in Saskatchewan` `income for the year`) (`the total of the credits` `credits`))

§§ `s 39 -- the Saskatchewan low-income tax credit, 2026`

-- s 39(5.2)(c)(i)-(iii): for 2026, B includes an amount L for the individual, the same for a qualified relation (a
-- cohabiting spouse, federal s 122.5(1)), and the same where the individual has no qualified relation but claims the
-- federal eligible-dependant amount (s 118(1)(b)) for a qualified dependant. L for 2026 is "[the amount calculated in
-- accordance with subclause (b)(i) x 1.05] and is adjusted in accordance with subsection 51(5)": not stated in the Act.
-- Reg 7 s 3 states it, as the numerator of D: "$460" (L in s 39(6.3) for 2026 is "the amount calculated in accordance
-- with subclause (5.2)(c)(i)"). NOTES.md finding 3.
`the 2026 s 39 base amount` MEANS 460

-- s 39(5.2)(c)(iv): for qualified dependants other than the one counted under (iii): "(A) [X] if: (I) the amount set out in
-- subclause (iii) is included ...; or (II) the amount set out in subclause (iii) is not included ... and the individual has
-- only one qualified dependant ...; and (B) two times the amount set out in paragraph (A) if the amount set out in subclause
-- (iii) is not included ... and the individual has two or more qualified dependants". So at most two child amounts count
-- (NOTES.md finding 5). X for 2026 is the 2025 figure "x 1.05 ... adjusted in accordance with subsection 51(5)", not stated
-- in the deposited text: an input.
GIVEN `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2026 s 39 child amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 39 amount B for 2026` `has a qualified relation` `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` `number of qualified dependants` `the 2026 s 39 child amount` MEANS
    LET `(iii) applies` MEANS (NOT `has a qualified relation`) AND `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` AND `number of qualified dependants` AT LEAST 1
        `others` MEANS IF `(iii) applies` THEN `number of qualified dependants` MINUS 1 ELSE `number of qualified dependants`
    IN       `the 2026 s 39 base amount`
        PLUS (IF `has a qualified relation` THEN `the 2026 s 39 base amount` ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `(iii) applies` THEN `the 2026 s 39 base amount` ELSE 0)
        PLUS (IF `others` AT LEAST 1
              THEN IF `(iii) applies` OR `others` EQUALS 1
                   THEN `the 2026 s 39 child amount`
                   ELSE 2 TIMES `the 2026 s 39 child amount`
              ELSE 0)

-- s 39(6.3) with Reg 7 s 3: "for the 2026 taxation year, the amount C is equal to 3.029% of the amount, if any, by which the
-- individual's adjusted income for that taxation year exceeds the amount D calculated in accordance with the following
-- formula: D = $54,532 - $460 / 0.03029". (Adjusted income: federal s 122.5(1), the individual's and the qualified
-- relation's income together; an input.)
`the 2026 s 39 reduction rate` MEANS 3.029%
`the 2026 s 39 amount D` MEANS 54532 MINUS (460 DIVIDED BY 0.03029)

GIVEN `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 39 amount C for 2026` `adjusted income` MEANS
    `the 2026 s 39 reduction rate` TIMES (`the excess of` `adjusted income` `over` `the 2026 s 39 amount D`)

-- s 39(4): "A = 1/4 x (B - C)"; s 39(3): that amount "is deemed to be an amount paid by an individual on account of the
-- individual's tax payable ... during each of the months specified" where the individual "(a) is an eligible individual;
-- and (b) has filed a return of income for the taxation year". The text has no "if any" on B - C; a negative A is read as
-- nil (NOTES.md finding 4). s 39(3.1): a shared-custody parent gets "1/2 x (A + B)", B being A calculated as if the
-- individual had no qualified dependants for whom they are a shared-custody parent.
GIVEN `amount B` IS A NUMBER, `amount C` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 39(4) quarterly amount` `amount B` `amount C` MEANS (`the excess of` `amount B` `over` `amount C`) DIVIDED BY 4

GIVEN `eligible individual under federal s 122.5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has filed a return of income for 2026` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a qualified relation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `number of qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `of them, shared-custody dependants` IS A NUMBER
      `adjusted income` IS A NUMBER
      `the 2026 s 39 child amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 39 low-income tax credit for each specified month` `eligible individual under federal s 122.5` `has filed a return of income for 2026` `has a qualified relation` `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` `number of qualified dependants` `of them, shared-custody dependants` `adjusted income` `the 2026 s 39 child amount` MEANS
    IF `eligible individual under federal s 122.5` AND `has filed a return of income for 2026`
    THEN LET `A` MEANS `the s 39(4) quarterly amount` (`the s 39 amount B for 2026` `has a qualified relation` `claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` `number of qualified dependants` `the 2026 s 39 child amount`) (`the s 39 amount C for 2026` `adjusted income`)
             `remaining dependants` MEANS `the excess of` `number of qualified dependants` `over` `of them, shared-custody dependants`
             `A without the shared-custody dependants` MEANS `the s 39(4) quarterly amount` (`the s 39 amount B for 2026` `has a qualified relation` (`claims the federal eligible-dependant amount for a qualified dependant` AND `remaining dependants` AT LEAST 1) `remaining dependants` `the 2026 s 39 child amount`) (`the s 39 amount C for 2026` `adjusted income`)
         IN IF `of them, shared-custody dependants` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN (`A` PLUS `A without the shared-custody dependants`) DIVIDED BY 2
            ELSE `A`
    ELSE 0

-- s 39(7): "the months specified for a taxation year are July and October of the immediately following taxation year and
-- January and April of the second immediately following taxation year." s 39(8), (9) apply federal s 122.5(3.1), (3.2)
-- with "$7": if the amount for the first specified month is less than $7 (and it is reasonable to conclude each later one
-- will be too), the year's total is deemed paid in that first month. One payment per quarter as a list of (month, year,
-- amount); a month is numbered 1-12.
DECLARE `Payment` HAS
    `month`  IS A NUMBER
    `year`   IS A NUMBER
    `amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment`
`a payment in` m y `of` a MEANS `Payment` WITH `month` IS m, `year` IS y, `amount` IS a

GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER, `quarterly amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Payment`
`the s 39 payments` `taxation year` `quarterly amount` MEANS
    IF `quarterly amount` EQUALS 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `quarterly amount` LESS THAN 7
         THEN LIST (`a payment in` 7 (`taxation year` PLUS 1) `of` (4 TIMES `quarterly amount`))
         ELSE LIST (`a payment in` 7 (`taxation year` PLUS 1) `of` `quarterly amount`),
                   (`a payment in` 10 (`taxation year` PLUS 1) `of` `quarterly amount`),
                   (`a payment in` 1 (`taxation year` PLUS 2) `of` `quarterly amount`),
                   (`a payment in` 4 (`taxation year` PLUS 2) `of` `quarterly amount`)

§§ `ss 40, 75, 81 -- filing, paying, and protection of the refund`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the individual`
    `a creditor of the individual`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file the return of income`
    `pay the tax as estimated`
    `charge, assign, garnish, attach, seize or set off the low-income tax credit refund`

-- s 75: "sections 150, 150.1 and 151 of the federal Act apply for the purposes of this Act": the Saskatchewan return goes
-- with the federal one, by the federal "filing-due date" (for an individual, federal s 150(1)(d) -- a borrowed date, an
-- input). s 81: where no instalments are required, the individual "on or before the individual's balance-due day for the
-- taxation year, shall pay to the minister the individual's tax as estimated pursuant to section 151 of the federal Act"
-- ("balance-due day", s 2(d), as defined federally: an input). Days are counted from 31 December of the taxation year.
-- Filing is required when tax is payable (federal s 150(1)(d)(i): "every individual who ... has tax payable"); the
-- individual who has no tax payable may still file, and must file to get the s 39 credit (s 39(3)(b)).
GIVEN `taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `has tax payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing-due date` IS A DATE
      `the balance-due day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to file and pay` `taxation year` `has tax payable` `the filing-due date` `the balance-due day` MEANS
    IF `has tax payable`
    THEN    (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `file the return of income`
             WITHIN `the filing-due date` MINUS (Date 31 12 `taxation year`)
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "no return filed by the filing-due date (s 75, adopting federal s 150)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `pay the tax as estimated`
             WITHIN `the balance-due day` MINUS (Date 31 12 `taxation year`)
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "tax not paid on or before the balance-due day (s 81(b))")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 40(1): "the amount of a refund that arises pursuant to section 38 or 39: (a) cannot be charged or given as security;
-- (b) subject to the regulations, cannot be assigned, garnished or attached; (c) is exempt from execution and seizure; and
-- (d) cannot be retained by way of deduction or set-off pursuant to The Financial Administration Act, 1993." (2): "Subsection
-- (1) does not affect or restrict: (a) the application of subsection 164(2) of the federal Act [applying a refund against
-- other amounts the individual owes] ... with respect to refunds that arise pursuant to section 39; or (b) the garnishment
-- or attachment, pursuant to the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act (Canada) as a result of the
-- application of subsection 164(1.4) of the federal Act, of refunds that arise pursuant to section 39."
GIVEN `the refund is applied under federal s 164(2) to another amount I owe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refund is garnished for family support under the federal Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40(2) lets the refund be taken` IF
        `the refund is applied under federal s 164(2) to another amount I owe`
    OR  `the refund is garnished for family support under the federal Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act`

-- The prohibition of s 40(1), as a rule on any creditor, outside the s 40(2) cases. It runs while the refund is
-- outstanding; `days` is the window looked at.
GIVEN `s 40(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the protection of my low-income tax credit refund` `s 40(2) applies` `days` MEANS
    IF `s 40(2) applies`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `a creditor of the individual`
         SHANT `charge, assign, garnish, attach, seize or set off the low-income tax credit refund`
         WITHIN `days`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `a creditor of the individual` BECAUSE "a s 39 refund cannot be charged, assigned, garnished, attached, seized or set off (s 40(1))"
